<title>USA: N.C. tourism group opposes stadium funding plan.</title>
<headline>N.C. tourism group opposes stadium funding plan.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's Travel and Tourism Coalition urged lawmakers to reject a bill authorizing referendums in Forsyth and Guilford counties on a baseball stadium funding proposal.</p>
<p>The proposal would raise the sales tax on restaurant meals by one cent in the two counties. Revenues from that tax and from a surcharge on baseball tickets would be used to pay debt service on $140 million worth of stadium bonds.</p>
<p>In a memo to lawmakers on Thursday, the coalition said the proposal would place an unfair burden on the restaurant industry and its customers.</p>
<p>&quot;The people subject to this tax, many living on fixed income, would pay a truly staggering sum to subsidize a private, professional baseball team,&quot; the memo said.</p>
<p>The North Carolina House is expected to vote on the proposal next week.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
